# Copy to the folder that holds agent2/, swarn-backend/ and swarn-frontend/
# (the compose build context) as `.dockerignore`, otherwise every build
# ships the virtualenvs, node_modules and old runs (tens of GB) to Docker.
#
# Order matters: Docker applies the LAST matching rule, and a rule that matches
# a parent folder counts. The allow-list must come first so the exclusions
# below still win inside the three repos.
*
!agent2
!swarn-backend
!swarn-frontend

**/.git
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.agents
**/.claude
**/.github
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
agent2/runs
agent2/sessions
agent2/workspace
agent2/knowledge
agent2/artifacts
agent2/agent/runs
agent2/agent/workspace
swarn-backend/work
swarn-frontend/coverage
